<title>SOUTH KOREA: Chung Ho Computer buying back shares.</title>
<headline>Chung Ho Computer buying back shares.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Chung Ho Computer Co Ltd said it would buy back 120,000 common shares on the open market from September 9 to December 7 to boost its share price.  </p>
<p>The company currently holds none of its own common shares.</p>
<p>The buyback represents 3.9 percent of Chung Ho's share capital, a company statement said. It added that the shares would be bought at the previous day's closing price. Daewoo Securities will handle the buyback.</p>
<p>Chun Ho's shares closed at 35,400 won per share on Wednesday, up 100 won on the day.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
